{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "58", "S": "03"}}, "news": [{"title": "Court stays hold up action against Aravali encroachments, CEC told", "para": "The state of Haryana encounters significant hurdles in tackling Aravali land encroachments following demolition efforts. A series of court cases and new violations are complicating enforcement actions significantly. The action taken report reveals ongoing legal challenges, with several structures left unaffected due to court stays and unresolved litigation. Supreme Court mandates stress the necessity of forest land restoration and reforestation initiatives for ecological recovery.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/court-stays-hold-up-action-against-aravali-encroachments-cec-told/133669228?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-223638/133669228.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Thiruvananthapuram corporation plans AI push to recover \u20b9200 crore in property tax arrears", "para": "The Thiruvananthapuram corporation is set to harness artificial intelligence for enhancing property tax recovery efforts. Aiming to reclaim around 200 crore rupees in overdue payments, the initiative will prioritize outstanding dues from government agencies and public establishments. By leveraging technology, the corporation seeks to efficiently pinpoint defaulters and optimize the recovery process, ultimately boosting financial stability and enhancing service delivery.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/thiruvananthapuram-corporation-plans-ai-push-to-recover-200-crore-in-property-tax-arrears/133669137?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-207148/133669137.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}, {"title": "Master plan first priority for Mangaluru\u2019s development: Muda\u2019s new chairperson", "para": "In his recent address, Santhosh Kumar Shetty, the newly appointed Muda chairperson, outlined his vision for future developments in Mangaluru. He stressed the importance of the Master Plan to guide the city's growth and expand its infrastructure, particularly enhancing road networks and flyovers to ease traffic congestion. Furthermore, he proposed affordable housing initiatives and streamlined regulations to empower residents, aiming to eliminate middlemen and promote direct engagement with the public.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/master-plan-first-priority-for-mangalurus-development-mudas-new-chairperson/133669102?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-236492/133669102.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}